-- ==============================================
-- FILE: restore_disenchant_ids.sql
-- GENERATED: 20260802210000
-- ==============================================
-- Nothing could be disenchanted, because almost nothing carried a disenchant id.
--
-- Spell::EffectDisEnchant returns without a word when item_template.disenchant_id
-- is 0, so the attempt simply did nothing - no message, no failure, nothing.
--
-- Of 26009 items in the running database, 535 had a value. The upstream dump,
-- sql/base/tw_world_item_template.sql, carries 8933. The data was not missing from
-- the project, it was lost here - presumably when this database was restored from
-- a full dump rather than built from sql/base.
--
-- So this restores rather than invents. The values come straight from that file.
-- Grouped by value, which turns 8404 single-row updates into 36 statements.
--
-- Only rows that currently hold 0 are touched. 0 items already carry a value that
-- differs from upstream's; those are left exactly as they are, since a deliberate
-- local change is indistinguishable from a stale one and overwriting would be the
-- riskier guess.


